Package: fan-controllerd
Architecture: linux-any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: drive-temperature fan controller daemon for an ESP32-C3 board
 Reads hard-drive temperatures from the kernel drivetemp hwmon, maps the hottest
 drive through a configurable piecewise-linear curve, and commands fan speed
 over USB serial to an ESP32-C3 running the matching firmware from this project.
 .
 Airflow survives the daemon itself. The controller holds its own failsafe and
 forces the fan to full speed whenever the host stops sending commands, so a
 crashed, stopped or disconnected daemon cannot leave a drive array without
 cooling. The daemon also cross-checks the duty the controller reports against
 the duty it asked for, watches the tachometer for a stalled fan, and reports
 each drive against its own rated and critical limits.
 .
 The drivetemp kernel module is required and there is no fallback temperature
 source, so this package arranges for the module to be loaded at boot.
 .
 The service is installed but left disabled. /etc/fan-controllerd.toml ships
 with placeholder device and disk identifiers, which have to be replaced with
 the ones for this machine before the daemon can do anything useful.
